<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander IV of Macedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">323–c. 309 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander IV was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roxana">Roxane</a>, born after his father's death in 323 BCE. He was proclaimed joint king with his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-arrhidaeus">Philip III Arrhidaeus</a>, but real power lay with the generals who fought over the empire. Held in custody at Amphipolis by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassander">Cassander</a>, he was murdered with his mother around 310 BCE, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty">Argead dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-iv-of-macedon.jpg" alt="Alexander IV of Macedon" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E. A. Wallis Budge (1857-1934) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexandros_IV_Aigos_Budge.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
